police say Teen Mom 2 star Jenelle Evans  made up the story about her husband  shooting and killing their French  Bulldog nugget for publicity in a press  release from the Columbus County  Sheriff's Office in Whiteville North  Carolina police say Janelle contacted  them on April 29th and advised them that  her husband David Eason had shot their  dog after it bit their two-year-old  daughter Ansley in the face police  conducted a search of the couple's  property but found no blood or physical  evidence to validate the animal had been  fatally injured there when they  questioned Evans a day after the search  her account of the incident changed and  she said she no longer wanted to  continue with the investigation the  statement reads in part Jenelle's stated  that the reason she filed the animal  cruelty report was for the publicity and  because she did not know where her dog  was the Columbus County Sheriff's Office  has closed the investigation against  Eason and no charges will be filed in  this case where we gonna do as a result  of the incident Janelle was fired from  the MTV reality show  MTV have previously ended their  relationship with David in February 2018  after he posted a number of homophobic  and transphobic tweets
 

